ticles/alaska-moho-model-reproducible-research-with-containers/alaska-moho-model-reproducible-research-with-containers.md","thumbnail":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-78ff0365c6ab7e190bfd281567cda948.png"},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"div","class":"uwtn-banner","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/banner-78ff0365c6ab7e190bfd281567cda948.png","key":"RErSU80XDi","urlSource":"figures/banner.png"}],"key":"GyXntIhJKJ"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/c468a06e88/build/MohoSurfaceGradient--20ad9c3d312e88f841005eee3da11370.png","key":"gPdhb3C2KB","urlSource":"figures/MohoSurfaceGradient-ClusteredGrids.png"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"fuvEjFx81M"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Making your research reproducible means that you provide the entire workflow from data, through software and post-processing freely available. Not only can somebody repeat your experiments and verify them, they can build upon them. In lab-based disciplines, there are many further challenges, but in research that is predominantly based on data processing, this ought to be an achievable goal.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"nkJQeA9YjA"}],"key":"EW6g1WiCUC"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We are releasing all of the background for our recent paper on the Alaska Moho (Miller & Moresi, 2018) to make it transparent and reproducible. Open source software is one thing but it is also important to make the software easily accessible: the software and raw moho picks are available through","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"ENeXWS4wry"}],"key":"UywXUeiqFF"},{"